@title STORY • NIA: THE ONE WHO STAYS
@bg skate_park_day
You're Nia Washington. Defensive mid. Oakland. Skater. Sneakerhead. Professionally unbothered. Unofficially, deeply bothered.
You liked Tyler since August. You told one person. Riley. Your best friend since you were nine.
Now Riley's at his house. And you're at the skate park, eating a whole bag of hot chips about it.
@show simone
Simone: (sitting down) I heard.
Nia: I'm fine.
Simone: You're eating hot chips at 9 a.m.
> [Sweet] "...I'm not fine." -> a1
> [Bitchy] "Hot chips are a breakfast food, Simone." -> a2
*a1
@add Self 3
Simone doesn't say anything. She just takes a chip. Then another. You finish the bag together.
@jump a_done
*a2
Simone: Mm-hm. And that's your third bag.
*a_done
@bg dorm_hallway_night
@show riley
Riley's outside your door. She looks like she's been crying.
Riley: Can I come in?
> [Good] Let her in. -> b1
> [Bold] "Say it from the hallway first." -> b2
*b1
@add Riley_Bond 2
She sits on your bed and doesn't say anything for a long time. Then: "I'm sorry." You let her sleep over anyway. You always do.
@jump end
*b2
@add Self 2
@add Riley_Bond 2
Riley: (through the door) I'm sorry. I knew. I'm an idiot. I'll never do it again. Can I please come in? I brought pancake mix.
You open the door. Of course you open the door.
*end
Nia Washington acts like nothing gets to her. The truth is, she's the one who always stays, even when it hurts.
